1
00:00:01,220 --> 00:00:06,053
There's a shark in the Arctic right now that may be older than the United States.

2
00:00:06,123 --> 00:00:08,090
It's the Greenland shark.

3
00:00:08,173 --> 00:00:12,067
And it can live for around four hundred years.

4
00:00:12,140 --> 00:00:20,577
Scientists aged them using the centre of their eyes, which forms before birth and never changes.

5
00:00:20,647 --> 00:00:24,566
The oldest one they measured was nearly four hundred years old.

6
00:00:24,636 --> 00:00:27,676
They grow about one centimetre a year.

7
00:00:27,926 --> 00:00:32,170
They aren't ready to have babies until they're around a hundred and fifty.

8
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:35,514
They swim slower than you walk.

9
00:00:35,584 --> 00:00:40,081
Many are half blind, because a parasite lives on their eyes.

10
00:00:40,151 --> 00:00:41,121
And yet...

11
00:00:41,171 --> 00:00:45,050
remains of polar bears have been found in their stomachs.

12
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:47,789
Their meat is toxic.

13
00:00:48,064 --> 00:00:52,696
Eaten fresh, it can make people stagger like they're drunk.

14
00:00:52,768 --> 00:00:56,504
Somewhere in the dark, one of them was already old...

15
00:00:56,554 --> 00:00:58,167
when the Titanic sank.
